id: "vuln-gitlab-oauth-plugin-695ce63f"
languages: ["java"]
severity: "ERROR"
message: "The GitLab OAuth plugin is vulnerable to session fixation."
metadata:
  cve: "CVE-2019-10371"
  cwe: "CWE-384, CWE-863"
pattern: >
  (HttpSession) request.getSession(false)
  if (session != null) {
    session.invalidate();
  }
  request.getSession(true);

pattern-not: >
  (HttpSession) request.getSession(false)
  if (session != null) {
    session.invalidate();
  }
  request.getSession(false);

This rule detects the vulnerable behavior of the GitLab OAuth plugin, which allows an attacker to steal the user's session by invalidating the current session and creating a new one. The "pattern" field specifies the vulnerable pattern, and the "pattern-not" field specifies the patched pattern.

